## Conventions

- PR titles and commit subjects must be Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `feat!:`, `chore:`, ...). PRs are squash-merged, so the PR title becomes the commit subject{% if 'release-please' in modules %} and drives release-please versioning{% endif %}.{% if 'pr-title' in modules %} CI validates both (fleet-ci's pr-title job + validate-commit-names).{% endif %}
- CI gates on the required check `all-green`: a check run the managed `.github/workflows/all-green.yml` verdict workflow creates after judging each CI run's jobs{% if not private %} plus the expected Copilot review of the head{% endif %} (the gate jobs themselves run centrally through repo-platform's fleet-ci.yml; `all-green` is the ruleset's SOLE required check). This repository's own test/lint jobs belong in `.github/workflows/checks.yml` (repo-owned, called inside the gate); do not edit ci.yml or all-green.yml, template sync overwrites them.{% if 'release-please' in modules %} The `info-release` job runs on top of the gate (`needs: [checks, ci]`; its `info-` name keeps the release pipeline out of the verdict), calling the managed release pipeline in `.github/workflows/release.yml`; this repository's release preparation (packaging, asset uploads, note edits) goes in the repo-owned `.github/workflows/update-release.yml` hook it calls.{% endif %}
- No typographic look-alike characters (curly quotes, em-dashes, invisible unicode). CI enforces this with the check-typography action; use plain ASCII punctuation.

